  "tagline": "GPL in-memory relational engine from SoftMethod that aimed for search-engine speed with SQL; abandoned ~2010.",
  "description": "BlackRay was a relational data engine that SoftMethod GmbH developed with Deutsche Telekom from around 2005 and released as open source in 2008-2009 under the banner 'the open source data engine'. It kept data in memory with search-engine-style indexing so that wildcard and text lookups over large tables stayed fast, while still offering SQL, JDBC and ODBC drivers, transactions and version-controlled persisted snapshots. It was licensed under GPLv2, written mainly in C++, and shipped builds for Linux, Solaris and macOS. The last release, 0.10.0, dates from 2010, the project domain was parked by late 2011, and only the SourceForge archive remains.",
